From 515e77f0bce1333ed18fdfc8e1e869827a704029 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 05:47:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(catalog): add a GitHub traffic collector

GitHub only shows repository traffic to accounts with push access and only
keeps the last 14 days, so the SIG cannot gather these numbers itself.

Add tools/github_traffic/github_traffic.py, which reads the documented
traffic endpoints (views, clones, popular referrers and paths) with a token
taken from the environment, merges each 14-day window into CSV files that
keep the full history, and can publish them to a GitHub Gist the SIG can
ingest without a privileged token. Repositories can be listed explicitly,
read from a file, or enumerated from an org (public, non-archived, non-fork
repositories the token can push to). It handles pagination, primary and
secondary rate limits and transient errors, and only needs the Python
standard library.

Add a daily GitHub Actions workflow that runs it once a token secret and a
Gist ID are configured, plus documentation and unit tests that run against
a fake transport.

Closes #53
